    "description": "Contract to National Library of Medicine - NLM/NIH \n- Developed Profiles in Science sites in Ruby on Rails, JavaScript, and MySQL (Amazon RDS). It gives Librarians ability to create online exhibits using both internal and external resources through the IIIF API.\n- Developed NLM Digital Repository in Ruby on Rails, Java, JavaScript, and Python. The site has millions of digital items with friendly interface, Section 508 compliance, and responsive support.\n- Developed, managed, and migrated 3 other web applications to the AWS Cloud: FDA Notices of Judgment, NLM FindingAids (Archivesspace), and IIIF Image server. \n- Integrated millions of books, videos, and records to work seamlessly in a Java repository system.\n- Awards: National Library of Medicine Excellent Award in 2013 (preserved scanned historic books), 2015 (redesigned the Digital Collections), 2016 (integrated born digital data), 2017 (Exhibits Builder tool), 2018 (FDA Notices of Judgment site), 2019 (Profiles in Science sites), and 2022 (Migration of applications to the AWS Cloud).",
